Chapter: PciProbe
  cites Diag chapter DiagPci
  cites Kernel chapter Pci
  cites Works chapter GopDraw
  cites Works chapter GopQr
  cites Kernel chapter BitmapFont
  cites Works chapter GopHandoff

 The bus walk, the classification, the BAR map verdict and the QR body live
 in Diag chapter DiagPci since 2026-08-18, where the diagnostic ladder's pci
 stage reads them; this chapter is the one-question image that paints them.

 We say:

Section: Halt

  pp-halt : Integer -> Integer
  pp-halt (n) = pp-halt (n + 1)

Section: Rendering

  pp-row : Integer, Integer, CbfFont, Integer, Integer, Integer, Text, Integer -> Integer
  pp-row (base) (stride) (font) (x) (y) (scale) (s) (col) =
    gop-draw-text base stride font x y s col scale 0

 gop-draw-text does not stop at the right edge: an overrun wraps to column
 zero of the row below and lands on top of whatever is there. That is why
 the identity and the detail are two lines at two scales rather than one.

  pp-callout : Integer, Integer, CbfFont, Integer, Integer, Text, List PciDevice, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  pp-callout (base) (stride) (font) (hs) (y) (label) (devs) (n) (kind) =
    let i = pp-find devs n 0 kind
    in if i < 0 then pp-row base stride font 40 y hs (label & "  NONE FOUND ON ANY BUS") 16711680
    else pp-callout-hit base stride font hs y label (list-at devs i)

  pp-callout-hit : Integer, Integer, CbfFont, Integer, Integer, Text, PciDevice -> Integer
  pp-callout-hit (base) (stride) (font) (hs) (y) (label) (d) =
    let a = pp-row base stride font 40 y hs (label & "  " & pp-line d) (pp-colour d)
    in pp-row base stride font 40 (y + 20 * hs) 1 (pp-tail d) (pp-colour d)

  pp-list : Integer, Integer, CbfFont, List PciDevice, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  pp-list (base) (stride) (font) (devs) (n) (i) (y0) (rows) (lcols) =
    if i >= n then 0
    else if i >= rows * lcols then 0
    else let d = list-at devs i
    in let x = 40 + (i / rows) * 300
    in let t = pp-row base stride font x (y0 + (int-mod i rows) * 18) 1 (pp-line d) (pp-colour d)
    in pp-list base stride font devs n (i + 1) y0 rows lcols

Section: The Codes

 A module rendered two pixels wide does not survive a photograph: at
 scale 2 on a 1280x800 screen the decoder found the finder patterns and
 read none of the codes. So scale 2 is not offered, and the codes are
 sized before the screen is divided rather than squeezed into a fixed
 band afterwards: the block takes the largest of 6, 5, 4, 3 that fits
 the space below the callouts, and the device list gets whatever is
 left. A fixed half-screen band cost two scale steps and silently
 truncated the list to four rows on a six-device machine.

  pp-fits : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Boolean
  pp-fits (w) (avail) (cn) (s) =
    let pitch = 45 * s + 24
    in let cols = (w - 40) / pitch
    in if cols < 1 then False
    else ((cn + cols - 1) / cols) * pitch <= avail

  pp-qh : Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  pp-qh (w) (cn) (s) =
    let pitch = 45 * s + 24
    in let cols = (w - 40) / pitch
    in if cols < 1 then 0
    else ((cn + cols - 1) / cols) * pitch

  pp-qs : Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  pp-qs (w) (avail) (cn) =
    if pp-fits w avail cn 6 then 6
    else if pp-fits w avail cn 5 then 5
    else if pp-fits w avail cn 4 then 4
    else 3

  pp-qr : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, CbfFont, Text, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  pp-qr (base) (stride) (w) (qy) (qs) (font) (body) (total) (cn) =
    let cols = (w - 40) / (45 * qs + 24)
    in let warn = if qs < 4 then "  SCALE 3: SHOOT CLOSE AND SQUARE" else ""
    in let t = pp-row base stride font 40 (qy - 22) 1 ("QR: " & show cn & " codes, " & show total & " bytes, scale " & show qs & ". Photograph every one." & warn) (if qs < 4 then 16776960 else 16777215)
    in pp-qr-chunks base stride qy qs cols body total cn 0

  pp-qr-chunks : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Text, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  pp-qr-chunks (base) (stride) (qy) (qs) (cols) (body) (total) (cn) (i) =
    if i >= cn then 0
    else let from = i * 100
    in let len = if total - from > 100 then 100 else total - from
    in let m = qr5-encode-part (show (i + 1) & "/" & show cn & ";") body from len
    in let d = qr-draw base stride (40 + (int-mod i cols) * (45 * qs + 24)) (qy + (i / cols) * (45 * qs + 24)) qs m
    in pp-qr-chunks base stride qy qs cols body total cn (i + 1)

Section: The Screen

  pp-count-line : Integer, Integer -> Text
  pp-count-line (n) (shown) =
    if shown >= n then "devices=" & show n & "  all listed  bus 0 and every bridge below"
    else "devices=" & show n & "  ONLY " & show shown & " FIT ON SCREEN -- THE QR CODES CARRY ALL " & show n

  pp-draw : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, CbfFont, List PciDevice, Integer -> Integer
  pp-draw (base) (w) (h) (stride) (font) (devs) (n) =
    let hs = if w >= 1024 then 2 else 1
    in let y0 = 100 + 3 * (24 * hs + 22) + 10
    in let body = pp-body devs n
    in let total = text-length body
    in let cn = (total + 99) / 100
    in let qs = pp-qs w (h - y0 - 40) cn
    in let qh = pp-qh w cn qs
    in let qyr = h - qh - 10
    in let qy = if qyr < y0 + 26 then y0 + 26 else qyr
    in let space = qy - 26 - y0
    in let rows = if space < 18 then 0 else space / 18
    in let lcols = (w - 40) / 300
    in let cap = rows * lcols
    in let shown = if n > cap then cap else n
    in let bg = gop-fill-rect base stride 0 0 w h 1710638
    in let t0 = pp-row base stride font 40 40 hs "PCI PROBE" 65535
    in let t1 = pp-row base stride font 40 70 hs (pp-count-line n shown) (if shown < n then 16711680 else 16777215)
    in let c1 = pp-callout base stride font hs 100 "NIC    " devs n 2
    in let c2 = pp-callout base stride font hs (100 + 24 * hs + 22) "STORAGE" devs n 1
    in let c3 = pp-callout base stride font hs (100 + 2 * (24 * hs + 22)) "USB    " devs n 12
    in let l = pp-list base stride font devs n 0 y0 rows lcols
    in pp-qr base stride w qy qs font body total cn

Section: Entry

  opening : [Device.Port, Device.Mmio] Integer
  opening =
    let base = boot-fb-base 0
    in let w = boot-fb-w 0
    in let h = boot-fb-h 0
    in let stride = boot-fb-stride 0
    in let font = cbf-init
    in act
      ri <- runtime-init 0
      let devs = pp-collect 0 0 []
      in let d = pp-draw base w h stride font devs (list-length devs)
      in pp-halt 0
    end
